The 1916–17 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 29th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1910/celtic1917.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1916-17|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> They won the league for the 4th year in a row, by ten points over nearest rival [[Greenock Morton F.C.|Morton]].

The Scottish Cup, which Celtic held as champions, was suspended for the third season in a row because of [[World War I]].

Celtic successfully defended their [[Glasgow Cup]] and [[Glasgow Charity Cup|Glasgow Merchants' Charity Cup]] trophies as well as the League.

